    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6234" root="جم" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُمَّانِىٌّ</span></b> , with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span>, (S,) an irreg. rel. n., applied
to a man, (Sb, S,) <i>Having a long</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُمَّة</span>: (S, K:)
or <i>having a great and long</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُمَّة</span>: (Sb, TA:) but
if you name a person <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُمَّة</span>, the rel. n. formed from
it is ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُمِّىٌّ</span></b>  (Sb, S) only. (Sb, TA.)


